   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     55,
     70
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests for {@link TaiInstant}. <p>TAI (International Atomic Time) counts uninterrupted SI seconds from its epoch of 1958-01-01T00:00:00(TAI). Internally a {@code TaiInstant} is stored as (taiSeconds, nanos), where nanos is always normalised into the range [0, 999_999_999]. <p>Key reference constants used throughout these tests: <ul> <li>{@code MJD_TAI_EPOCH = 36204} — Modified Julian Day of 1958-01-01 (TAI epoch)</li> <li>{@code MJD_UNIX_EPOCH = 40587} — Modified Julian Day of 1970-01-01 (Unix epoch)</li> <li>{@code TAI_OFFSET_AT_TAI_EPOCH = 10} — TAI was 10 s ahead of UTC when TAI started</li> <li>{@code UNIX_SECONDS_AT_TAI_EPOCH = -378691200} — Unix timestamp (s from 1970-01-01) of the TAI epoch (1958-01-01), i.e. {@code -(MJD_UNIX_EPOCH - MJD_TAI_EPOCH) * 86400}</li> </ul>"
   },
   {
